# Tactical Roadmap

The phased twelve-month sequence of the approved platform: signature moments balanced against an always-on presence, every tactic an Activation Card placed by date, channel, audience, message, phase and KPI (key performance indicator).

**Not approved.** The owners and the calendar are a person's to approve, and no owner is recorded.

**Period and markets.** The campaign period is July 2026 through June 2027, ending no later than 30 June 2027, across the United States, the European Union and Sofia, Bulgaria.

## The phases

| phase | objective | months |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Pre-Seed | Prepare the proof base, public identity and approval route before The Stop Line reaches the market through Signed by Humans. | 1-3 |
| Launch | Introduce The Stop Line publicly through Signed by Humans and direct owners, technical buyers, partners and talent to approved proof. | 4-5 |
| Sustain | Keep The Stop Line visible between launch moments through proof, explanation, partner enablement and senior craft. | 6-9 |
| Amplify | Use approved proof and third-party credibility to widen The Stop Line without widening the AI (artificial intelligence) claim. | 10-12 |

Each major moment runs Tease → Launch → Sustain → Amplify; the corporate rollout overlay is Engage → Enhance → Advocate → Amplify.

