## The always-on loop

Underneath the phases runs the Conversation Management loop: establish goals → gather assets → develop proprietary content → deploy across owned, earned and paid → train advocates → deploy → measure → refine — supported by the always-on newsroom running proactive stories and reactive issues management.

## The proof-building order

Proof is built in the order the strategy can defend: first the cases and proof assets are cleaned, labelled and approved so The Stop Line has evidence to stand on; then thought leadership explains what the evidence means through Signed by Humans, founder posts, buyer explainers and senior craft stories; only after that does visibility widen through earned validation, partner activation, employee advocacy and paid amplification.

## The rollout

**First audience.** The year speaks first to owners of midsize businesses, led by Elena, because the owner-control message must be tested before it becomes the lead public story.

**Then widen.** After owners understand The Stop Line and Signed by Humans, the story widens to technical buyers, referral partners, ecosystem partners, enterprise buyers, professional influencers, employees and senior Sofia talent, each receiving the same proof-first platform adapted to their role.

