| Shared founder and senior craft content | No publishing owner is named yet; founders and senior spokespeople are named as voices, but the managing role is still unassigned. | Launch posts in Months 5 and 8, then sustained posting and advocacy support through Months 9-11. | Social pack, spokesperson materials, proof-page links and approved message tracks. | Internal content production unless paid amplification is approved. |
| Paid testing and retargeting | No paid media owner is named yet. | Daily checks during paid activity and weekly headline KPI review. | Owner message test, UTM (Urchin Tracking Module tracking parameters) structure, paid search terms where used, proof-page destination and approved creative. | Out-of-pocket spend decided case by case after proof exists. |
| Earned validation and influencer outreach | No media relations owner is named yet. | Prepare in Launch, activate in Month 10 after proof exists, then review weekly during active outreach. | Proof page, fact sheet, approved spokesperson route, press release, partner proof pack and disclosure rules. | Internal media relations time; external services or events approved case by case. |
| Partner enablement | No partner-program owner is named yet. | Briefing push in Month 6, then monthly partner follow-up through Amplify. | Partner proof pack, event / experiential kit, approved reference stories and claim-compliance checks. | Internal partner enablement plus case-by-case event or production cost. |
| Conversation Management and Observatory newsroom | No always-on newsroom owner is named yet. | Daily listening and triage, weekly signal review and immediate escalation for crisis tripwires. | Q&A / FAQ, escalation route, crisis tripwire, do-not-say lines and approved answers. | Internal operating time; monitoring tools or external support approved case by case. |
| Measurement and executive scorecard | No measurement owner is named yet. | Paid checked daily, headline KPIs reviewed weekly and executive scorecard closed in Month 12. | UTM format, campaign identifier, baseline message testing, proof-page analytics, lead tracking and talent signals. | Internal measurement effort unless research, tools or paid reporting require separate approval. |

## Global to local

One core channel-agnostic toolkit travels across markets: The Stop Line platform, Signed by Humans signature, narrative, do-not-say lines, proof labels, approval route, message tracks, collateral templates and UTM format stay fixed, while local markets adapt hooks, spokespeople, language, local proof and market-specific tactics; global KPIs stay small and consistent, with local targets set from each market's baseline.

